<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Zealand First</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1993–</span> · Also known as NZ First</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> First is a nationalist and populist political party founded in 1993 by Winston Peters after he left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a>. It has held the balance of power in several parliaments under MMP, forming coalitions with National in 1996 and Labour in 2017 and joining National and ACT in government in 2023. It campaigns on immigration, pensions and economic nationalism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-zealand-first.jpg" alt="New Zealand First" width="320" height="138" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: New Zealand First · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Zealand_First_logo_2026.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
